## 1) Full Detailed Architecture

### 1.1 System Purpose
Web-Summariser is a multi-surface summarization platform that supports:
- Browser-side summarization through a Chrome extension
- Web app usage through a React client + Node backend
- Local AI summarization using FastAPI + Hugging Face models
- Cloud AI summarization using provider APIs (OpenAI, Gemini, Anthropic, Mistral, Groq)
- Local LLM summarization through Ollama
- Multi-format input processing (text, URL content, PDF, DOCX, images)

The system is designed to let users choose where inference runs:
- Local CPU/GPU pipeline (privacy-first, on-device)
- Local Ollama model
- Cloud provider model


### 1.2 Top-Level Components

A) Browser Extension (Chrome, Manifest V3)
- Path: extension/
- Core files:
  - manifest.json
  - background.js
  - content.js
  - sidebar.html
  - sidebar.js
- Role:
  - Captures page content from active tabs
  - Allows manual URL addition and content merging
  - Routes summarization requests to local FastAPI or cloud providers
  - Stores API keys and UI preferences in chrome.storage.local
  - Provides history and follow-up query interactions

B) Python Summary Service (FastAPI)
- Path: summary_service/
- Active entrypoint: main.py (running on port 5001)
- Role:
  - Local summarization API for text and file inputs
  - Extraction and OCR pipeline
  - Multi-model routing (BART, T5, LexRank, Combined)

C) Node/Express Backend (Auth + Conversations + Chat Orchestration)
- Path: server/
- Entrypoint: server.ts (port 5000)
- Role:
  - User auth/session/token APIs
  - Chat history persistence (conversations/messages)
  - Folder APIs
  - Gemini API orchestration and model fallback logic
  - Proxy to FastAPI summarization for summarize intents

D) React Frontend Client
- Path: client/
- Toolchain: Vite + React + TypeScript
- Role:
  - App UI for auth, dashboard, chat/folders/history experiences
  - Calls Node backend APIs via configured API base URL

E) Data Layer
- MySQL via Sequelize in server/database.ts
- Models:
  - users
  - conversations
  - messages
  - uploads (folder model currently maps to uploads table)

F) Legacy/Alternate Artifacts
- Extension_bridge/ appears to be an alternate/older extension bridge variant
- summary_service/main_backup.py contains older API behavior and additional endpoints not fully present in current main.py


### 1.3 Runtime Topology and Ports

Primary local ports:
- 5001: FastAPI summary service
- 5000: Express backend
- 5173: React client (dev)
- 11434: Ollama

Primary local URLs:
- FastAPI health: http://localhost:5001/health
- Express APIs: http://localhost:5000/websears/*
- React UI: http://localhost:5173
- Ollama tags/generate: http://localhost:11434/api/*


### 1.4 Connection Graph (Implemented)

Flow A: Extension local summarization
1. content.js extracts page text
2. background.js relays to sidebar.js
3. sidebar.js local route calls FastAPI:
   - POST http://localhost:5001/summarize
   - POST http://localhost:5001/summarize/selective
4. FastAPI returns summary payload
5. Extension renders structured output and stores history

Flow B: Extension cloud summarization
1. sidebar.js builds prompt
2. direct API calls from extension to provider endpoints:
   - OpenAI: https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions (model gpt-4o)
   - Gemini: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{candidate}:generateContent
   - Anthropic: https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages (claude-3-5-haiku-20241022)
   - Mistral: https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions (mistral-small-latest)
   - Groq: https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions (llama3-8b-8192)
3. Result rendered in extension

Flow C: Extension Ollama summarization
1. sidebar.js -> background message OLLAMA_FETCH
2. background.js performs fetch to Ollama endpoint
3. sidebar.js reads response from Ollama /api/generate with model llama3.2

Flow D: React client app APIs
1. Client uses VITE_API_BASE_URL and credentials include
2. Calls Express routes under /websears/*
3. Express validates auth token cookie for protected routes
4. Express uses MySQL via Sequelize for persistence

Flow E: Express chat summarize path
1. Client sends request to /websears/chat
2. If summarize intent detected, Express forwards to FastAPI /summarize with multipart form
3. Response is persisted in messages table
4. JSON response returned to client

Flow F: Express chat Gemini path
1. Client sends request to /websears/chat with text/file for AI reply
2. Express calls Gemini SDK with fallback candidate list
3. Resolved working model cached per API key
4. Response persisted and returned


### 1.5 Connection Mismatches to Be Aware Of

These are important for operational correctness:

1) FastAPI response shape mismatch for chat summarize
- Express /websears/chat currently reads summaryResponse.data.final_summary
- Current FastAPI main.py /summarize returns field summary (not final_summary)
- Risk: empty/undefined AI response in summarize branch

2) Missing FastAPI Ollama route expected by Express
- Express /websears/chat/ollama forwards to http://localhost:5001/ollama/summarize
- Current summary_service/main.py does not expose /ollama/summarize
- Risk: chat ollama route fails at runtime

3) Model naming differences across layers
- FastAPI local model IDs: distilbert-cnn, t5-small/t5, lexrank, combined
- Extension UI badges sometimes refer to bart/t5/lexrank/combined and provider-style model strings
- Keep mapping table explicit when integrating new routes


