### 1.8 Image, OCR, and Document Processing Architecture

Image handling currently present in active FastAPI main.py
- Routes image file through extract_text_from_file -> _extract_text_from_image
- Uses PIL preprocessing (grayscale, median filter, contrast, brightness, optional sharpen retry)
- Uses pytesseract for OCR
- Uses TESSERACT_CMD or system PATH auto-discovery
- Returns readable text or meaningful fallback string if no text detected

Document handling
- PDF: pypdf extraction in active main.py
- DOCX: python-docx extraction if installed
- TXT: UTF-8 decode with ignore fallback

Additional modules present but not directly wired in current main.py
- pdf_handler.py
  - richer pypdf/pdfplumber extraction metadata and quality checks
- image_analyzer.py
  - transformer-based image captioning pipeline (BLIP)
  - structured image summary payload

This means the codebase supports two image/document design directions:
- OCR-first extraction (active in main.py)
- Vision-caption analysis module (available as optional integration)


