### 1.10 Security and Auth Architecture

Auth method
- Cookie-based JWT token named token
- Signed with JWT_SECRET and 1-day expiration
- Middleware checks req.cookies.token and verifies payload

OAuth
- Passport Google strategy (if GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET set)
- Passport Facebook strategy (if FACEBOOK_APP_ID/SECRET set)
- Callback sets JWT cookie and redirects to client dashboard

CORS/session
- Express CORS currently allows origin http://localhost:5173 with credentials true
- Session middleware enabled in Express

Secrets in use
- JWT_SECRET
- DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASS
- GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL
- FACEBOOK_APP_ID, FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET, FACEBOOK_CALLBACK_URL
- GEMINI_API_KEY (optional server-side fallback)
- TESSERACT_CMD (optional for OCR executable path)


### 1.11 How To Add New Models

A) Add a new local FastAPI summarization model
1. Create model wrapper module in summary_service/ (e.g., my_model.py)
2. Import function in summary_service/main.py
3. Add model ID mapping inside summarize_text router
4. Add model metadata in /models route
5. Update extension model dropdown options for local provider if needed
6. Validate timeout and chunking behavior for long inputs

B) Add a new cloud provider in extension
1. Add provider key in ALL_PROVIDERS (sidebar.js)
2. Add UI input field for API key in settings panel
3. Implement callProvider function similar to callOpenAI/callMistral
4. Register in CLOUD_CALLERS map
5. Add host_permissions in extension/manifest.json for provider domain
6. Add model options in select controls

C) Add a new Ollama model
1. Pull model locally (example: ollama pull <model>)
2. Update callOllama payload model field in sidebar.js or expose model select
3. Optionally add server-side route parity if using /websears/chat/ollama orchestration

D) Add vision model inference in FastAPI
1. Integrate image_analyzer.py functions into active main.py routes
2. Add endpoint for image caption/analysis separate from OCR extraction
3. Return structured fields: short_summary, detailed_analysis, image_info


### 1.12 Operational Runbook

Recommended startup order
1. Start FastAPI: uvicorn main:app --reload --port 5001 (in summary_service)
2. Start Express: npx ts-node server.ts (in server)
3. Start React client: npm run dev (in client)
4. Optional local LLM: ollama serve and pull needed model
5. Load extension folder in chrome://extensions

Health checks
- FastAPI: GET /health
- Express: open any /websears route with valid auth flow
- Ollama: GET /api/tags


