## 2) Compact Architecture (Short but Enough)

### 2.1 What This Project Is
A hybrid summarization platform with four active layers:
- Chrome Extension (capture + summarize)
- FastAPI Summary Service (local models + OCR/file parsing)
- Express Backend (auth, chat history, Gemini orchestration)
- React Client (web UI)

### 2.2 Core Connections
- Extension local summary -> FastAPI at :5001
- Extension cloud summary -> direct provider APIs
- Extension Ollama -> background fetch to :11434
- React client -> Express at :5000 (/websears/*)
- Express summarize path -> FastAPI /summarize
- Express stores users/conversations/messages in MySQL

### 2.3 Models In Use
- Local: BART (distilbert-cnn route), T5, LexRank, Combined
- Cloud: OpenAI gpt-4o, Gemini fallback list, Anthropic Claude Haiku, Mistral Small, Groq Llama3 8B
- Ollama: llama3.2

### 2.4 Inputs Supported
- Plain text
- Website extracted text
- PDF
- DOCX
- TXT
- Images (OCR pipeline)
- Manual URL merge + follow-up question over summary

### 2.5 Libraries (High Level)
- Python: FastAPI, Transformers, Torch, Sumy/NLTK, pypdf/pdfplumber, Pillow, pytesseract, python-docx
- Backend: Express, Sequelize, MySQL2, Passport, JWT, Multer, Axios, Google Generative AI SDK
- Frontend: React, Vite, Tailwind, Radix UI, Zod, React Hook Form

### 2.6 What You Can Add Next
- New local model in FastAPI router
- New cloud provider in extension caller map + host permissions
- New Ollama models by changing model in payload or adding UI selector
- Vision caption endpoint by wiring image_analyzer.py into active main.py

### 2.7 Important Current Gaps
- Express expects final_summary from FastAPI summarize; active FastAPI currently returns summary
- Express /websears/chat/ollama expects FastAPI /ollama/summarize; active FastAPI route is not present

These two should be aligned for fully reliable end-to-end behavior.

